  "position": 4,
  "source": {
   "type": "exam",
   "ref": "practice-exam-u2 Q4 (Practice exam 2)"
  },
  "facet": "written",
  "prompt": "Visceral motor regions are located on the ________ aspect of the developing neural tube and move to the _______ aspect in the mature brainstem.",
  "format": "choice",
  "choices": [
   "Ventral; medial",
   "Dorsal; lateral",
   "Ventral; lateral",
   "Dorsal; medial",
   "Inferior; superior"
  ],
  "accept": [],
  "require_side": false,
  "tags": [
   "written",
   "practice-exam-u2",
   "unit:u2",
   "kind:theory",
   "source:practice-exam",
   "modality:motor"
  ],
  "answer": "Ventral; lateral",
  "explain": "In the embryonic neural tube, motor columns lie ventrally in the basal plate and sensory columns dorsally in the alar plate, separated by the sulcus limitans. When the tube opens out at the fourth ventricle, the walls rotate laterally, so visceral motor nuclei end up lateral to the somatic motor nuclei, and sensory nuclei lie lateral to both."
 },
 {
