   "written",
   "practice-exam-u2",
   "unit:u2",
   "kind:theory",
   "source:practice-exam",
   "modality:autonomic"
  ],
  "answer": "Post-ganglionic parasympathetic nuclei",
  "explain": "Brainstem nuclei contain the preganglionic parasympathetic neurons (for example Edinger-Westphal and the dorsal motor nucleus of the vagus). The postganglionic parasympathetic neurons sit in peripheral ganglia (such as the ciliary or pterygopalatine ganglion) or in the walls of target organs, outside the brainstem. Post- is Latin for after, and ganglion is Greek for knot or swelling."
 },
