  "facet": "written",
  "prompt": "Because visceral afferent fibers from the heart enter the spinal cord at T1– T4, where is cardiac ischemic pain commonly referred?",
  "format": "choice",
  "choices": [
   "Right lower quadrant",
   "Left arm and chest",
   "Groin",
   "Posterior scalp",
   "Periumbilical region"
  ],
  "accept": [],
  "require_side": false,
  "tags": [
   "written",
   "practice-exam-u2",
   "unit:u2",
   "kind:theory",
   "source:practice-exam"
  ],
  "answer": "Left arm and chest",
  "explain": "Visceral afferents from the heart enter the cord at T1 to T4, the same segments that receive somatic sensation from the chest wall and medial left arm. The brain misattributes the visceral signal to the somatic dermatomes that share those dorsal horn neurons, so cardiac ischemia is felt in the left arm and chest. This is called referred pain."
 },
