  "answer": "All of the above",
  "explain": "Keyed answer of the practice exam. Strictly, retinal ganglion cell axons go directly to the lateral geniculate nucleus (conscious vision), the superior colliculus (orienting), the pretectum (pupillary light reflex) and the suprachiasmatic nucleus (circadian rhythm). The primary visual cortex is reached only through the LGN and the optic radiations (Lecture 11), so it is not a direct target."
